# One rule, on purpose. The seal in `artifacts/evidence-manifest.json` records
# `content_sha256` over the *raw bytes* of every tracked file, so a file whose
# line endings depend on the cloner's `core.autocrlf` gives that fingerprint a
# value nobody else can reproduce -- including from a clone of the very commit it
# describes.
#
# This was a per-suffix list, and the list lost three times: `*.mjs`, `*.yml` and
# `*.toml` had to be appended when eslint and the packaging config arrived, `.yaml`
# was never covered at all, and an extensionless file (`LICENSE`, `MANIFEST.in`,
# `.gitignore`, this file) could not be covered by a suffix in the first place.
# Measured at 0.4.15: five tracked files were ungoverned, and a fresh clone
# differed from the working tree in three of them.
#
# `text=auto` still detects binaries by content, so an image added later is left
# alone without needing a line here.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Trellis journals are append-only; workspace indexes retain normal merge rules.
.trellis/workspace/*/journal-*.md merge=union
